    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Man and environment are closely linked. Early humans depended on nature, but with tools and technology people now change the environment through farming, industry and cities. This brings both benefit and harm.\nHuman activities cause deforestation, soil erosion, air and water pollution and climate change. Different regions show different lives, such as the Eskimos in cold lands and the Bedouins in deserts, which show how people adapt to their surroundings.\nSustainable development means meeting present needs without harming the future. We can save the environment by planting trees, saving water and energy, and reducing waste."
    }
